<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belsky family</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Belskys were a princely family descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algirdas">Algirdas</a>, Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, through his son Vladimir, and named after their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> of Bely. Prince Fyodor Belsky fled from Lithuania to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in 1482 and married a niece of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a>, giving the family high rank among the boyars. During the minority of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a>, Ivan Fyodorovich Belsky led the court from 1540 until the rival Shuiskys overthrew him in 1542; the senior line died out in 1571.</p></div>
